# Licensing

This repository is deliberately split. The schema and the tooling are open so that
Standards can be a reference other people build against; the catalogue is the product.

| What | Licence | File |
|---|---|---|
| The schema and public project documentation (`schema/*.md`, root Markdown, `.github/`, and Markdown under `mcp/`, `workflow/`, and `evaluation/`) | CC BY 4.0 | `LICENSE-SCHEMA` |
| The tooling (`schema/compile.py`, `schema/*.html`, `mcp/server.py`, Python and JSON schemas under `workflow/`, Python under `evaluation/`, `examples/workflow/reference_loop.py`, and `tests/`) | MIT | `LICENSE-CODE` |
| Synthetic evaluation inputs (`evaluation/conditions/`, `evaluation/fixtures/`) and original workflow briefs/reference content (`examples/workflow/` except `reference_loop.py` and the embedded font software described below) | CC BY 4.0 | `LICENSE-SCHEMA` |
| Public Sans and DM Mono WOFF2 font software embedded in retained workflow HTML, plus its notices | SIL Open Font License 1.1 | `examples/workflow/reference/font-licenses/` and the embedded licence metadata |
| **Instrument** — the free flagship (`packs/instrument/`) | CC BY 4.0 | `packs/instrument/LICENSE` |

Everything in this repository is covered by one of the three licences above.

The rest of the catalogue — Broadsheet, Raw, Agitprop, Contra and Cornice — is proprietary
and is not published here. So are the proof grids, the handoff pack and the commercial
material. © 2026 Applied Form. All rights reserved.

## Why this split

The schema is the argument, and an argument nobody can adopt is not a standard. Opening it
costs a licence fee that was never going to be charged and buys the position of reference
implementation. Instrument is open for the same reason it is free: a system installed as
somebody's default is worth more than a system sold once.

The other five are the catalogue, and the catalogue is what is for sale. They live in a
separate repository, which is why this one is safe to read end to end.

## Attribution

For the CC BY 4.0 material, attribute as: *Standards by Applied Form —
https://github.com/Applied-Form/standards-schema*

## Note

Every system in this repository extends a design tradition. No organisation's marks,
logotypes or identities are reproduced, and nothing here is affiliated with or endorsed by
any institution referenced. Instrument names its open-licence typefaces in
`packs/instrument/SOURCE.md`. The Instrument pack itself contains no font binaries. Retained
workflow HTML embeds Public Sans and DM Mono WOFF2 files for offline reproduction under
their SIL Open Font License 1.1 notices.
